dog eating a chameleon.  After I ascended, I was able to say things to
myself like "boy, I could have done that without so many
genocides/polymorphs/etc." and I eventually did with other characters.  I
think that the most important thing is the first ascension, after that, more
come slightly more easily.  For example, when I first started, unless I got
a wish in minetown, I was dead before sokobon.  Now I've succeeded with 2
characters that didn't have wishes until the quest or below.  Nethack is
just a game with a huge learning curve, getting your first ascension is
really tough, the rest fall into place more easily, and before you know it,
you're trying to play illerate atheist foodless genoless wishless polyless
tourists etc.

So I guess what I'm saying is that there is no need to feel dumb, people who
have ascended start seeing things differently and sometimes downplay their
ascensions, when in reality any ascension is quite an accomplishment




